WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.416 --> 00:00:04.983
At the center of AI is data,
it powers everything.

00:00:04.983 --> 00:00:07.690
And at Microsoft,
we have unique data graphs.

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.620
World knowledge with Bing and

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.640
work knowledge with the rest
of the Microsoft graph.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.680
But really the magic
happens when you make sense

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.620
of all this information.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.775
We've evolved from
simple searches and

00:00:18.775 --> 00:00:22.060
keyword matching to using
advanced AI techniques,

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.820
like machine reading
comprehension that uses deep

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.920
learning to understand
the meaning behind words.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.820
We also need really
powerful hardware in order

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:34.310
to process these AI models,
like deep neural networks.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:37.580
We've partnered with Intel to
create industry leading agility

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:41.800
and performance with FPGA chips
that allow us to read and

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.330
understand billions of
documents in milliseconds.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.678
So how does this apply
to you every day?

00:00:47.678 --> 00:00:51.070
Today, I'm gonna show you how
AI enables intelligent search

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.310
in a few ways.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:54.930
One with intelligent answers,
Bing for

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.840
business, intelligent
image search, and

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.130
a new search paradigm that is
for more conversational search.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.990
Let's start with
something rather mundane,

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.490
like finding a movie to
watch for the holidays.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:09.250
So inside of a simple keyword
search, I'm gonna use something

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:14.356
with more natural language,
like movies directed by

00:01:14.356 --> 00:01:19.770
Spielberg starring Tom Hanks,
let's use Tom Hanks.

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:24.930
Okay, this answer is
specific to my actual query.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.660
It filtered out TV shows and

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.470
their other partnerships, but
it still included a movie

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.180
that they're doing
together in January.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:35.220
With Bing's vast understanding
of the world, people and

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.560
entities, and
how they relate to each other,

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:41.770
AI enables us to power more
rich and complete answers.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:46.200
Now let's say I'm doing
research on something

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:48.250
a bit more controversial.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:51.370
I'm a vegan and I take a lot
of plaque from my family for

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:53.480
being an annoying kill pusher.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.940
I wanna be prepared for

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.510
the inevitable holiday table
debate with my cousin.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:03.033
So I'm gonna do a search for

00:02:03.033 --> 00:02:06.890
facts about Kale.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:10.070
This result here is
a multi-source answer.

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.730
Bing uses AI to bring
together information from

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.800
multiple different
websites into one place.

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.250
And at Microsoft, we believe
it's important to understand

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:20.240
where information comes from.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.325
So although we provide quick
access and links to content,

00:02:23.325 --> 00:02:27.090
we're also really careful to
ensure we also include sources.

00:02:27.090 --> 00:02:30.780
So this way I can feel confident
about my advocacy of kale.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.480
And if I want to be
super prepared and

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.150
understand both sides of
an issue, because we don't

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:39.730
live in a world of absolutes,
I can do a query like,

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:44.060
also using natural language
like, is kale good for you?

00:02:47.320 --> 00:02:49.940
This is a multi-perspective
answer.

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.972
Bing shows alternate viewpoints,
so

00:02:51.972 --> 00:02:54.516
that you can understand
both sides of an issue.

00:02:54.516 --> 00:02:58.270
So on one side I have pro kale
and on the other side I have

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:01.452
a cautionary tale of why
too much kale is bad.

00:03:01.452 --> 00:03:03.139
So that I don't have
to live in a bubble,

00:03:03.139 --> 00:03:04.890
where everything about
kale is amazing.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:09.220
And if I really wanna embrace
this kale loving lifestyle,

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:12.210
I should probably take
up yoga or pilates.

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:15.120
But I don't actually really know
the difference between them.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:21.719
So if I do a search for,
difference between yoga and

00:03:21.719 --> 00:03:25.770
pilates, I get this
comparison answer.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:30.060
Bing has taken comparisons
a feature typically found

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.420
in product or
shopping based scenarios, and

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.350
have expanded it to
a wider query set.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:38.658
We use machine reading
comprehension to read the web

00:03:38.658 --> 00:03:41.515
and understand entities and
their aspects,

00:03:41.515 --> 00:03:44.611
in order to compare
differences between items.

00:03:44.611 --> 00:03:48.382
So this yoga seems like
it's more of my jam, so

00:03:48.382 --> 00:03:51.303
let's go ahead and
just pick that.

00:03:51.303 --> 00:03:55.785
And I've heard a lot about yoga
retreats in Costa Rica, but

00:03:55.785 --> 00:04:00.010
I don't actually have a sense
for how big is Costa Rica.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.300
This is a relational answer.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.245
In addition to showing
the actual square miles,

00:04:07.245 --> 00:04:10.620
I'm also told it's about twice
the size of Massachusetts,

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:12.480
which is incidentally
my home state.

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:15.165
So I have a good sense
of what that means.

00:04:15.165 --> 00:04:19.545
Bing has used AI and add some
perspective into information, so

00:04:19.545 --> 00:04:22.455
not only we're using AI to
search across the billions

00:04:22.455 --> 00:04:23.580
of documents in the web,

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:27.595
we're also using AI to make
information more understandable.

00:04:27.595 --> 00:04:30.435
Because while the engineer may
geeks out of all this data,

00:04:30.435 --> 00:04:33.535
the designer only knows that
real user delight comes from

00:04:33.535 --> 00:04:34.805
making data make sense.

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:39.100
So all of these new experiences,
multiple sources,

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:42.390
multiple perspectives,
comparisons, and relational

00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:46.390
answers, they all make up what
we call intelligent answers.

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:50.370
So all of these everyday AI
capabilities are awesome, but

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:53.220
what if we could apply them
to the context of work.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:55.359
That's exactly what we've
done with Bing for Business.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:58.485
For starters, let me just go
back to the Bing homepage.

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:03.170
Because I'm signed in with
my Microsoft work account,

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:06.560
at the bottom of my home page,
I can see industry related news

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.750
that's relevant to me,
a person in tech.

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:11.510
And beyond this personalization,

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.240
let me show you what
the Microsoft graph and

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:16.160
AI can do for
workplace productivity.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.340
So I have a Microsoft
holiday party coming up,

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:23.820
and the fabulous Harry Shum is
my executive vice president.

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:27.230
So because I'm signed in and I
have Bing for Business enabled,

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:29.500
I type in Harry's org.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:33.036
And note that I'm not using his
last name, but it still provides

00:05:33.036 --> 00:05:36.311
me with the org chart for the
right Harry, even though there

00:05:36.311 --> 00:05:39.277
are plenty of great Harry's
that work at Microsoft.

00:05:39.277 --> 00:05:43.504
Also in the same experience web
results that are related to

00:05:43.504 --> 00:05:45.152
the query Harris org.

00:05:45.152 --> 00:05:45.739
So Bing for

00:05:45.739 --> 00:05:48.875
Business brings together
the best of corporate Internet

00:05:48.875 --> 00:05:52.150
search with the best of web
search all into one experience.

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:56.158
So if I do something a little
bit more complicated like,

00:05:56.158 --> 00:06:00.710
how much vacation do I get?

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:07.746
Because of the FPGA chip,
I get answers in milliseconds.

00:06:07.746 --> 00:06:12.373
And if it's for
something super obscure,

00:06:12.373 --> 00:06:16.495
I can search for,
can I hire a cousin?

00:06:16.495 --> 00:06:19.589
Machine reading comprehension
powers this answer.

00:06:19.589 --> 00:06:22.815
What you'll notice here is that
cousin isn't even mentioned

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:23.691
in the passage.

00:06:23.691 --> 00:06:26.598
That's because Bing knows that
cousin is a family member and

00:06:26.598 --> 00:06:28.879
understands the meaning
behind words to give me

00:06:28.879 --> 00:06:30.620
the right answer.

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:34.810
Not that I would hire my
kale-hating cousin anyway.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:36.450
So for this holiday party,

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:38.720
I'm also gonna wanna find
something festive to wear.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:41.440
But it is a work event,
so I'm gonna search for

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.420
work appropriate
holiday cocktail dress.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.960
And I'm gonna go to image,
our image vertical.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.490
And then, this one looks
appropriately festive.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:53.810
Bing intelligent image
uses computer vision,

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:56.660
an AI technique, in order
to find dresses that look

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:59.620
just like this one with
direct links to buy.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:02.520
So that I can look around and
do some price comparisons.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:05.240
And the other thing it does, is
our object detection allows me

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:08.470
to rescope this query
on just this necklace.

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:12.710
So now I can find necklaces that
look very similar to one in this

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.630
photo, again with
direct links to buy.

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:18.150
Bing is intelligent search
that saves time and money.

00:07:19.555 --> 00:07:23.470
Okay, in addition to Intelligent
Answers, Bing for Business, and

00:07:23.470 --> 00:07:26.810
Intelligent Image Search,
we're also using AI

00:07:26.810 --> 00:07:30.380
to make the search box itself
more conversational with

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:32.980
an interactive guided
search experience.

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:35.810
We hear a lot from customers
that they wish search

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:37.320
could just complete
their sentences.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:44.240
If I do a vague search like,
I'm feeling stressed,

00:07:44.240 --> 00:07:45.950
which may or
may not be because of this demo.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:50.200
I get this guided
search experience.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:53.070
So I get obviously the web
results you'd expect from

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.220
a search engine.

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:59.160
I get our answers, but then
up top, what you'll see here

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.580
is that it prompts for
additional career refinements.

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:05.550
So I can go through and
pick stress management and

00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:07.560
then breathing exercises, and

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:11.220
then I can also kind of expand
to see previous results.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.850
What's different here is
that search is building upon

00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:16.230
the last search.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.955
So it's a little bit
more conversational,

00:08:17.955 --> 00:08:19.820
a little bit more personalized.

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:24.600
We're able to do with this is
get you better answers faster.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.770
This is a new search paradigm.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.459
We are amplifying our extensive
knowledge graph with AI.

00:08:30.459 --> 00:08:34.732
Our expertise in conversational
AI with our bots like and

00:08:34.732 --> 00:08:37.685
Zoe are brought together
with our vast data,

00:08:37.685 --> 00:08:41.569
enables Bing to create a new
interactive search experience

00:08:41.569 --> 00:08:44.068
that gets you better
answers faster.

00:08:44.068 --> 00:08:47.898
If I do another example for,
let's see,

00:08:47.898 --> 00:08:53.050
Seattle verse, I'm prompted for
popular rivalries.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:55.310
So I'm gonna select
the Rams here.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:58.080
And then here you'll see
an answer of an upcoming

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.460
game on the 17th.

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:01.200
In addition to web links and

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.940
this awesome answer, I can also
see who Bing predicts to win.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:07.770
So we're predicting that
the Rams will win by 51%.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:11.840
Bing uses search, social and

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:14.680
other relevant data signals in
order to make predictions on

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:18.130
sports, reality TV shows and
more.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:23.754
And if I do another
really ambiguous search,

00:09:23.754 --> 00:09:26.130
like set default.

00:09:26.130 --> 00:09:29.480
Without any context of what
default I'm trying to set,

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:32.280
I'm prompted with
very popular things

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:33.680
that people set default for.

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:38.310
Conversational search uses
large-scale machine learning, so

00:09:38.310 --> 00:09:41.380
this experience is only
gonna get better over time.

00:09:41.380 --> 00:09:44.940
AI learns from user engagement,
so we're really excited for

00:09:44.940 --> 00:09:47.260
the future of
conversational search.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:50.690
What I've shown you today,
Intelligent Answers, Bing for

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:53.300
Business, Intelligent
Image Search, and

00:09:53.300 --> 00:09:57.370
a new conversational guided
search is just a small sampling

00:09:57.370 --> 00:10:01.060
of how we are using AI to
create intelligent search.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:03.910
All of these experiences
are either live today or

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:05.020
starting to roll out today.

